    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup today is anchored by **Jonathan Aranda**, our strongest start with a 67.01 efficiency score. Facing a favorable 4.55 xERA matchup against Lugo, **Jonathan Aranda** benefits from a distinct platoon advantage (+12%) and the high-leverage context of the #2 spot, making him our premier candidate to contribute across the counting stats. **Bryson Stott** (62.69) and **Yainer Diaz** (62.13) also grade as elite options. While **Bryson Stott** draws a tough task against the stuff of Cade Cavalli, his dynamic platoon boost of 13% keeps his floor high, whereas **Yainer Diaz** remains a priority start despite the pending lineup confirmation, given the 4.62 xERA of Melton.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was sidelining **Jung Hoo Lee**, who fell just short of the \"Strong\" start threshold with a 47.52 score. His matchup against Springs is hampered by a significant 10% platoon penalty, which prevented him from cracking the starting nine. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Masyn Winn**, who sits at a 56.13 score; while he faces the formidable Zac Gallen, the efficiency model heavily weights his speed profile, as his 100% stolen base opportunity index adds critical value in a category that remains our primary focus.\n\nManagers should note that both **Yainer Diaz** and **Geraldo Perdomo** are currently tracking under \"Lineup Pending\" designations. Should their official slots shift downward in the batting order, their respective scores will be adjusted, though **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2019s 60.48 score suggests he will remain a viable asset at the UTIL spot regardless of minor fluctuations. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the statuses of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Tyler Freeman**, all of whom remain unavailable due to injury or scheduling gaps, leaving the heavy lifting to our active core of **Cal Raleigh**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Lawrence Butler**.",
